# Checklist Design & Anti-Slop UI Rules

When designing, building, or refactoring UI components, pages, or user flows:

1. **Anti-Slop Rule**:
   - **NEVER use decorative pill-shaped eyebrow badges, kicker pills** (`rounded-full`, pastel backgrounds, sparkle icons, uppercase tracking-wide text) above headings, heroes, cards, or sections. Headings must start cleanly and directly.

2. **Core Design Enforcements**:
   - **Accessibility**: WCAG 2.1 AA contrast, visible focus rings, aria-invalid, screen reader alt text.
   - **States**: Explicitly build Default, Hover, Active, Focus, Disabled, Loading, Empty, and Error states.
   - **Mobile Touch Targets**: Minimum 44x44px touch areas and proper keyboard inputs.
